412 Calculation Modeling

413 All calculations are conducted in Cartesian coordinates x, y, and z. To 414 align crystallographic a, b, and c, the x- and y-axes correspond to the a- 41s and b-axis, and z = x × y due to the nonperpendicular c-axis in a 416 monoclinic cell (position vector r = x + y + z), i.e., z = x × y. Such 417 transformation can also be expressed by a lattice matrix

\begin{equation}
\mathbf{L}=\begin{pmatrix}a&0&0\\ 0&b&0\\ c{\cdot}\cos\beta&0&c{\cdot}\sin\beta\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation}

