For periodic calculations such as piezoelectric of 1-RTP (see 419E 420 Supporting Information) or SHG susceptibility, the initial model was 421 obtained by SC-XRD results. Specifically, for SHG susceptibility, to 422 simultaneously investigate 1-RTP and 2-fold-disorder-contained 1- 423 HTP, the SHG calculations with the supercell approach were 424 conducted for 1 × 2 × 1 supercells of 1-RTP and 1-HTP. Supercells 425 of 2 × 1 × 1 and 1 × 1 × 2 of 1-HTP were also constructed to 426 validate the approximation. For each primary cell in the supercell of 1- 427 HTP, the disorder part with different occupancies was deleted to 428 depict the 2-fold disorder approximately.

429 For cluster models, Cartesian coordinates are defined as above, 430 with the original point shifted to the center of mass of the cluster. 431 Geometric optimizations were carried out for H atoms, with non- 432 hydrogen atoms fixed (due to the imprecise determination of 433 hydrogen atoms by SC-XRD). The Hamiltonian for self-consistent 434 field (SCF) iteration was based on hybrid PBE0 functional5,56 in 435 which Grimme's D3 dispersion correction57 with Becke-Johnson 436 (BJ) damping function58 (noted as PBE0-D3(BJ))was utilized to 437 improve the precision of computation. The basis set for describing the 438 wave function was def2-SVp.59 The optimization process was 439 conveyed with the GDIIS algorithm, where Hessian matrices were 440 calculated precisely at the first point.

